course: dictionary
lesson: 5570
title: The many meanings of lesson
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning the writer wants. The word lesson is a good example. «Today's lesson: sharing equally» means the topic you are taught that day.
explain: «That taught me a lesson» means you learned something from what happened to you, so you will be careful next time. Here lesson is about experience, not a school timetable.
explain: A lesson can also be a part of a book or course to study. Ask yourself: is someone teaching, is someone learning from a mistake, or is someone studying a book? The clues in the sentence point to the right meaning.
fact: A lesson is a time when you are taught something, such as a maths lesson.
fact: A lesson is something you learn from what happens to you.
fact: A lesson can be a part of a book or course to study.
fact: In «his mother's lessons», the bonobo Kanzi learned by watching, so lessons can happen without a classroom.
fact: A moral is the lesson a story teaches, as in «Everything's got a moral, if only you can find it.»
exercise: «Today's lesson: sharing equally.» What does lesson mean here? | A game played in the gym | A cold drink at break time | *The topic taught that day | A time to go home early
exercise: «That taught me a lesson.» What does lesson mean here? | A piano lesson | A part of a book to read | *Something learned from what happened | A maths test
exercise: In «his mother's lessons», the bonobo Kanzi learned by watching. What does lesson mean? | *Times when his mother taught him by showing | A list of words in a book | A lie told to friends | Breaks from school
test: «Everything's got a moral, if only you can find it.» In this sentence, what is a moral? | A type of cake | Something you forget quickly | A loud noise | *The lesson a story teaches
test: On a school timetable, what is a lesson? | A lunch with friends | A break in the playground | *A time when you are taught something, like maths | A test you have already passed
exam: Jayden writes, «That was a hard lesson.» What does he mean? | He ate his lunch too quickly | He read a hard book | He had a maths class that was hard | *He learned something from what happened
